      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "For patients with low back pain secondary to pathological motion of an unstable lumbar motion segment, interbody fusion may be indicated. Numerous open and minimally invasive techniques have been traditionally used, but all suffer from shortcomings related to biomechanics or inherent iatrogenic destabilization. A novel transaxial approach to the lumbosacral junction has recently been described which appears to obviate many of the limitations of previous techniques. Preliminary results of the transaxial approach to lumbosacral fixation appear promising."},
